                <pb facs="0673" n="565" xml:id="pg565"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Snowden to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received February 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 72.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose translated copy
                    of a communication from the Marquis of Vega de Armijo, minister of state, making
                    a formal tender to our Government of the caravel <hi rendition="#italic">Santa
                        Maria.</hi></p>
                <p>This reproduction of the vessel in which Columbus sailed in his voyage of
                    discovery to the New World is well constructed and cost the Spanish Government
                    over $30,000.</p>
                <p>The friendly considerations that induce His Majesty’s Government to make this
                    generous offer and the flattering terms employed in communicating its wishes,
                    must awaken the liveliest sentiments of appreciation on the part of our
                    Government and people.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Loudon
                    Snowden.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d549-a1.xml" xpointer="d549-a1"/>
            </div>
